# =============================================================================
# ArriveO'Clock environment variables
#
# The app runs FULLY — maps, search, driving routes, and the motion-based alarm
# — with this file completely EMPTY. Everything below is optional.
#
# Copy to `.env` to override. VITE_* vars are bundled into the browser (public
# only). Non-VITE vars are read only by the /api serverless functions.
# =============================================================================

# --- Supabase (optional: cross-device login + sync) ------------------------
# Without these the app stores data locally (per-device). The anon key is
# public and protected by Row-Level Security.
#   Project Settings → API
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- Service endpoint overrides (optional: only if you self-host) ----------
# Defaults are free public instances and need no key.
#   maps tiles  : OpenFreeMap   (hardcoded in src/config.js)
#   geocoding   : Photon        (https://photon.komoot.io)
#   driving     : OSRM          (https://router.project-osrm.org)
# VITE_GEOCODER_URL=https://photon.komoot.io
# VITE_OSRM_URL=https://router.project-osrm.org

# --- Transit routing backend (optional: read by /api/route.js) -------------
# For ETAs/distances that MATCH Google Maps, add a Google Directions API key
# (server-side only — never exposed to the browser). Enable "Directions API"
# in Google Cloud; the monthly free credit covers typical personal usage.
# GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
#
# Free alternative (no key): MOTIS via Transitous, used when no Google key is
# set. Coverage depends on open GTFS feeds; elsewhere the app falls back to a
# distance-based estimate (the live alarm stays accurate regardless, as it's
# motion-based). Override only if you self-host MOTIS/OpenTripPlanner.
# TRANSIT_API=https://api.transitous.org
